  moved_2nd: DeAngelis, Ratliff
summary:
- topic: FY2025 Superintendent’sBudget Overview
  text: The Board reviewed the proposed $69.5 million operating budget for the SOUTHPORTLANDSCHOOLDEPARTMENT,
    representing a 5% increase driven primarily by fixed employee compensation costs
    and a 3.8% tax mill rate increase.
- topic: Staffing Adjustments and COVID-19 Funding Loss
  text: Administration highlighted the fiscal challenges of losing $1.5 million in
    federal COVID-19 relief funds, forcing difficult staffing decisions and the reduction
    of several positions across the district.
- topic: Elementary and Middle School MTSS Implementation
  text: Elementary and middle school principals presented on the implementation of
    the Multi-Tiered Systems of Support (MTSS) for academic, behavioral, and social-emotional
    needs, emphasizing data-driven decisions using the new EDU climber platform.
- topic: SOUTHPORTLANDHIGHSCHOOL Progress and Belonging
  text: SOUTHPORTLANDHIGHSCHOOL reported positive trends in student belonging, increased
    teacher trust, a significant reduction in suspensions, and growth in dual enrollment
    and extended learning opportunities.
- topic: Multilingual Department Master Plan
  text: The Multilingual Department outlined its new master plan and language access
    initiatives, including a new inbound phone interpretation service to support the
    district's diverse student body.
- topic: McKinney-Vento Program and Housing Crisis
  text: The McKinney-Vento program update highlighted a doubling of doubled-up students
    due to the housing crisis and showcased the success of the new pilot grant preventing
    student homelessness.
- topic: Public Advocacy for High School Art Program
  text: During public comment, teachers and community members advocated strongly against
    the proposed elimination of a high school art teacher position, emphasizing the
    vital role of fine arts in student development and equity.
